#
# The worker image builds from the repo root (docker build -f worker/Dockerfile .)
# because the package imports as `worker.*`. That makes the whole repo the build
# context, so exclude everything the image has no use for — and, critically, the
# local virtualenv.
#
# worker/.venv is the sharp edge: the Dockerfile creates the environment with
# `uv sync` and then COPYs worker/ over it. Without this file a developer's host
# venv (wrong platform, absolute paths baked in) would clobber the container's and
# the image would fail at run time rather than build time.
worker/.venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Go build outputs and toolchain state — the image contains no Go.
bin/
build/
dist/
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Repo and IaC state, none of which belongs in an image layer.
.git/
.github/
deploy/
web/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.backup
.terraform/
